  "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/zizmorcore/zizmor/tarball/v1.32.0",
  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/zizmorcore/zizmor/zipball/v1.32.0",
  "body": "[Sponsorship is appreciated!](https://github.com/sponsors/woodruffw/)\r\n\r\n## New Features \ud83c\udf08[\ud83d\udd17](https://docs.zizmor.sh/release-notes/#new-features)\r\n\r\n- zizmor now has experimental support for GitHub Actions workflow lockfiles. Please see [the limitations documentation](https://docs.zizmor.sh/usage/#workflow-lockfiles) for more information about the current implementation and its limitations ([#2463](https://github.com/zizmorcore/zizmor/issues/2463))\r\n\r\n## Enhancements \ud83c\udf31[\ud83d\udd17](https://docs.zizmor.sh/release-notes/#enhancements)\r\n\r\n- zizmor's input collection is now \"root-aware\" by default, meaning that invocations like zizmor . will no longer collect inputs unless they would actually be used by GitHub Actions, etc. This should eliminate spurious findings from (e.g.) workflow definitions in vendored directories. See the [input collection](https://docs.zizmor.sh/usage/#input-collection) documentation for more information. ([#2454](https://github.com/zizmorcore/zizmor/issues/2454))\r\n\r\n- zizmor's LSP now honors the didChangeWorkspaceFolders event ([#2461](https://github.com/zizmorcore/zizmor/issues/2461))\r\n\r\n- zizmor's LSP now audits pre-commit inputs ([#2485](https://github.com/zizmorcore/zizmor/issues/2485))\r\n\r\n- zizmor now provides Windows ARM64 wheels on PyPI ([#2424](https://github.com/zizmorcore/zizmor/issues/2424))\r\n\r\n    Many thanks to [@ndabas](https://github.com/ndabas) for proposing and implementing this improvement!\r\n\r\n## Bug Fixes \ud83d\udc1b[\ud83d\udd17](https://docs.zizmor.sh/release-notes/#bug-fixes)\r\n\r\n- Fixed a bug where the [bot-conditions](https://docs.zizmor.sh/audits/#bot-conditions) audit did not properly flag if: condition of jobs that call a reusable workflow ([#2457](https://github.com/zizmorcore/zizmor/issues/2457))\r\n\r\n- Fixed a bug where the [obfuscation](https://docs.zizmor.sh/audits/#obfuscation) audit would incorrectly flag (and suggest an incorrect auto-fix for) expressions that constant-reduce to other expressions ([#2483](https://github.com/zizmorcore/zizmor/issues/2483))\r\n\r\n- Fixed a bug where the [template-injection](https://docs.zizmor.sh/audits/#template-injection) audit did not flag attacker-controllable contexts wrapped in fromJSON(...), such as fromJSON(toJSON(github.event.issue.title)) ([#2495](https://github.com/zizmorcore/zizmor/issues/2495))\r\n\r\n- Fixed a bug where the [template-injection](https://docs.zizmor.sh/audits/#template-injection) audit did not flag attacker-controllable contexts in the values of case(...), such as case(cond, github.event.issue.title, 'x') ([#2504](https://github.com/zizmorcore/zizmor/issues/2504))\r\n\r\n- Fixed a class of bugs in the [obfuscation](https://docs.zizmor.sh/audits/#obfuscation) audit where a constant-reducible subexpression would not be replaced with a contextually correct form ([#2483](https://github.com/zizmorcore/zizmor/issues/2483))\r\n\r\n- Fixed a bug where zizmor would incorrectly audit pre-commit inputs that ended with .yml, despite pre-commit requiring the .yaml suffix ([#2485](https://github.com/zizmorcore/zizmor/issues/2485))\r\n\r\n- Fixed a bug where zizmor would not honor some ignore comments for the [stale-action-refs](https://docs.zizmor.sh/audits/#stale-action-refs) audit ([#2494](https://github.com/zizmorcore/zizmor/issues/2494))\r\n\r\n- Fixed a bug where zizmor would not honor some ignore comments for the [ref-version-mismatch](https://docs.zizmor.sh/audits/#ref-version-mismatch) audit ([#2494](https://github.com/zizmorcore/zizmor/issues/2494))",
